/******************************************************************************************
* ToolboxEventTrigger                                                                     *
*                                                                                         *
* Method:                                                                                 *
* 1. Create the tasks class which is derived from ToolboxTask,                            *
*    in this example PollIdleExample.                                                     *
* 2. Leave Wimp_ENull unmasked.                                                           *
* 3. Call the tasks method setPollIdleInterval(int); passing the minimum interval         *
*    between null events before entering the pollIdle loop.                               *
* 4. Use the tasks runIdle() method inside the poll loop.                                 *
*                                                                                         *
* int main() {                                                                            *
*   PollIdleExample *task = new PollIdleExample();                                        *
*   task->initTask("<PollIdle$Dir>");                                                     *
*   task->setMask(256);                                                                   *
*   task->setPollIdleInterval(1);                                                         *
*   while (!task->quit) {                                                                 *
*     task->runIdle();                                                                    *
*   }                                                                                     *
*   delete task;                                                                          *
*   return 0;                                                                             *
* }                                                                                       *
*                                                                                         *
* 5. Create a nullReason() method in the tasks class.                                     *
* 6. Place ToolboxEventTrigger::eventDispatcher(); in the tasks method nullReason()       *
*    event handler.                                                                       *
*                                                                                         *
*  void PollIdleExample::nullReason() {                                                   *
*    ToolboxEventTrigger::eventDispatcher();                                              *
*  }                                                                                      *
*                                                                                         *
* 7. Derive a class from a Toolbox Window gadget and the constructor ToolboxEventTrigger, *
*    passing the WindowId, ComponentId, Event number and the Delay to the derived classes *
*    constructor and onto ToolboxEventTrigger. Note: the event number can be different to * 
*    an event configured for the gadget or can be a derived class from a gadget with no   *
*    events such as a Label.                                                              *
*                                                                                         *

*  MyLabel::MyLabel(int objectId, int componentId, int flags, int event, int delay) :     *
*    ToolboxLabel(objectId, componentId, flags),                                          *
*    ToolboxEventTrigger(objectId, componentId, event, delay) {}                          *
*                                                                                         *
* 8. Add an event handler to the derived gadget class.
*
*  MyLabel::eventHandler() {
*    do something here
*  }
*
* 10.In the MyWindow constructor 
* 9. Add an event handler to the derived window class which calls the derived gadget
*    event handler. Example with objects label1 and label2 of class MyLabel. 
*
*  MyWindow::eventHandler(int event) {
*    switch(event) {
*      case Event1:
*        label1->eventHandler();
*        break;
*      case Event2:
*        label2->eventHandler();
*        break;
*      default: break;
*    }
*  }
* The minimum interval passed to setPollIdleInterval must be a factor to that passed to   *
* the derived gadget class. Multiple derived gadgets or objects from derived gadgets are  *
* able to have different delays and/or event numbers                                      *
******************************************************************************************/
